Title: 0014-aros-system-window-border
Repository: pragtical
Base-Commit: 5c05f09e081833b581fb5ecd10e64963dec87f03
Requires: 0013-aros-current-directory-without-slash.patch
Author: aros-pragtical project
Date: 2026-11-16
Upstream-Status: local-only
Scope: AROS only, default of config.borderless in data/core/config.lua and the settings plugin.

Problem:
  The editor drew its own title bar and window buttons by default. On AROS the window then had no system border, could not be dragged or depth-arranged like other windows, and its drawn buttons behaved unlike Intuition gadgets.
Solution:
  Default config.borderless to false on AROS, so the window gets the Intuition border, drag bar and gadgets. The setting stays available.
Validation:
  2026-11-16, mainline nightly 20261113, AROS One 1.3 and Raspberry Pi nightly 20261110 in QEMU: the editor opens with the Intuition border and gadgets; drag bar, close gadget and iconify gadget work.
Removal:
  Permanent for the AROS port.

diff --git a/data/core/config.lua b/data/core/config.lua
index 3967cc3e..29e5875b 100644
--- a/data/core/config.lua
+++ b/data/core/config.lua
@@ -384,9 +384,10 @@ config.draw_whitespace = false
 ---When set to true, Pragtical draws its own window decorations,
 ---which can be useful for certain setups.
 ---
----Defaults to true.
+---Defaults to true, except on AROS, where the window gets the system's
+---own border and gadgets.
 ---@type boolean
-config.borderless = true
+config.borderless = PLATFORM ~= "AROS"
 
 ---Shows/hides the close buttons on tabs.
 ---When hidden, users can close tabs via keyboard shortcuts or commands.
diff --git a/data/plugins/settings.lua b/data/plugins/settings.lua
index 167da1c5..8facdc6a 100644
--- a/data/plugins/settings.lua
+++ b/data/plugins/settings.lua
@@ -496,7 +496,7 @@ settings.add("User Interface",
       description = "Use built-in window decorations.",
       path = "borderless",
       type = settings.type.TOGGLE,
-      default = true,
+      default = PLATFORM ~= "AROS",
       on_apply = function()
         core.configure_borderless_window()
       end
